                <pb facs="0785" n="697" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg697"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3531/119: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bliss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-01-25T17:00:00-05:00">January 25, 1933—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7. Your 9, January 18, 5 p.m. If you have not yet received the written reply from
                    the Minister of Foreign Affairs you are requested <pb facs="0786" n="698"
                        xml:id="pg698"/> to point out to him immediately that the continued delay of
                    the Argentine Government in granting to the United States the tariff reductions
                    of the Chilean-Argentine <hi rendition="#italic">modus vivendi</hi> is
                    occasioning discrimination against American commerce and to express the hope
                    that you will receive promptly a definite and favorable answer to your
                    representations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
